  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Start Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - We are almost done with our transformer! But first, we need to build a DECODER.
  - The DECODER is very similar to the ENCODER. But instead of encoding the sequence
    of input tokens, we make an encoding based on the possible output tokens and
    then use ATTENTION to check how similar the relations of the ENCODER are to the
    relations for the output tokens.
  - 'The DECODER starts of in the same way as the ENCODER: First create a POSITIONAL
    ENCODING, then pass the embedding through ATTENTION. Remember to create a duplicate
    of the embedding before ATTENTION for the RESIDUAL CONNECTION later on!'
  - After you make your initial ATTENTION embedding based on the output tokens, you
    have to add the RESIDUAL CONNECTION back in and NORMALIZE the result.
  - There are two different IMPORT buildings on this factory floor. One supplies
    the output embedding of the ENCODER you just made, which you will need later
    on. The other one has the output tokens which you will use for this first step.
